# Mac settings checks (advisory — mismatches WARN, not MISS).
# Format: label|kind|location|key|expected[|compare]
# kind: json-editor (cursor or code), defaults, sound-menu-bar-always,
#       machine-name-not-default, next-window-switch-key, chrome-json,
#       iterm-profiles, qbittorrent-vpn-interface
# location: editor id, "global" for NSGlobalDomain, Chrome profile dir
#           name (e.g. Default), profile display name (e.g. natera.com),
#           "*" / "@last" for Chrome's last-used profile, or "@all" for every
#           Chrome user profile
# compare: eq (default), at_most (numeric actual <= expected)
# In an interactive terminal gar offers to fix WARNs for json-editor,
# defaults, sound-menu-bar-always, next-window-switch-key, chrome-json, and
# iterm-profiles kinds. machine-name-not-default is advisory only.
# next-window-switch-key only applies when Karabiner Elements is installed
# and the Czech-QWERTY input source is enabled; it checks that "Move focus to
# next window" (symbolic hotkey 27) is Command-< (ASCII 92, keycode 50) — the
# expected binding on this layout. toggle-switch-key also toggles Command-`,
# but that is not the desired state for this check. The fix writes (92, 50,
# 1048576).
# chrome-json reads Preferences / Secure Preferences under
# ~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome; skipped if Chrome is not
# installed. Startup prefs are per profile — "*" checks the last-used one
# (the profile you pick in "Who's using Chrome?"). session.restore_on_startup=1
# is "Continue where you left off".
# iterm-profiles checks that iTerm has profiles named Default, Caution, and
# Midcaution — by name, across both "New Bookmarks" and any *.json under
# ~/Library/Application Support/iTerm2/DynamicProfiles; skipped if iTerm is
# not installed. The fix clones the current Default profile's settings into
# ~/Library/Application Support/iTerm2/DynamicProfiles/gar.json under the
# missing name(s) — Dynamic Profiles reload live, no iTerm restart needed —
# and is skipped if there's no Default profile to clone from.
# qbittorrent-vpn-interface checks that qBittorrent's Settings → Advanced →
# Network Interface is pinned to a VPN tunnel (utun*), not left on the
# default (all interfaces) — a killswitch measure so torrent traffic can't
# leak onto the raw connection if the VPN drops. Reads Session\Interface from
# ~/.config/qBittorrent/qBittorrent.ini (qBittorrent's real config store on
# this machine — not ~/Library/Preferences or ~/Library/Application Support,
# which hold only NSNavPanel state and runtime data respectively). Skipped if
# qBittorrent isn't installed. Advisory only, no automatic fix: the expected
# value is a pattern (utun*), not a fixed one, and qBittorrent rewrites this
# file on quit, so editing it while the app is running wouldn't stick.
# com.apple.keyboard.fnState: the fix writes the plist value immediately (so
# the check goes green right away), but System Settings' checkbox and the
# actual F-key behavior do NOT update until a full restart — a logout is not
# enough. This is a real macOS limitation (the write doesn't post the
# com.apple.keyboard.fnstatedidchange notification the Settings UI and
# keyboard driver listen for), not a gar bug — restart to see/feel it.
Cursor auto-save|json-editor|cursor|files.autoSave|onFocusChange
VS Code auto-save|json-editor|code|files.autoSave|onFocusChange
Keyboard repeat speed|defaults|global|KeyRepeat|2|at_most
Keyboard repeat delay|defaults|global|InitialKeyRepeat|15|at_most
Show all filename extensions|defaults|global|AppleShowAllExtensions|1
Use F1, F2, etc. as standard function keys|defaults|global|com.apple.keyboard.fnState|1
Always show volume in menu bar|sound-menu-bar-always||||
Machine name|machine-name-not-default||||
Move focus to next window (Command-<)|next-window-switch-key||||
Chrome On startup: continue where you left off|chrome-json|*|session.restore_on_startup|1
iTerm profiles (Default, Caution, Midcaution)|iterm-profiles||||
qBittorrent Network Interface bound to VPN|qbittorrent-vpn-interface||||
